course: dictionary
lesson: 10399
title: Tribute: respect or payment
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A tribute is something you say, do or give to show respect or thanks. Read the words around it: «The whole town came to pay tribute to the brave firefighters.» The clues are came, brave and firefighters, so tribute must mean a way of showing thanks.
explain: Tribute can also mean a payment. «In 1240 the Mongols destroyed Kyiv, and the lands of Rus paid them tribute, money and goods handed over every year.» The clues are money, goods and every year. Swap your meaning into the sentence: "paid them thanks" does not fit, so this is the payment meaning.
explain: One word can have more than one meaning. A tribute band copies the music of a famous band, and «The garden is a tribute to her hard work» means the garden shows how hard she worked. Always ask which meaning fits the sentence around it.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Tribute» means something said, done or given to show respect, thanks or admiration.
fact: «Tribute» can also mean money, food or goods that a weaker people paid to a stronger ruler.
fact: A tribute band copies the music of a famous band.
fact: «Pay tribute to» means to show respect or thanks for someone, especially after they have died or done something brave.
exercise: «The whole town came to pay tribute to the brave firefighters.» What does pay tribute mean here? | Put out the fire | Forget what they did | *Show respect and thanks | Pay them money for their work
exercise: In history, what was a tribute? | *Money, food or goods a weaker people paid to a stronger ruler | A song played at a concert | A present given on a birthday | A school prize
exercise: What is a tribute band? | A band that only plays at weddings | A band that has never played any music | A band made up of teachers | *A band that copies the music of a famous band
test: «The garden is a tribute to her hard work.» What does tribute mean here? | *It shows how good her hard work was | It is a song about gardens | It is a bill she must pay | It is the name of a dog
test: «The lands of Rus paid them tribute, money and goods handed over every year.» Which words show that tribute was a payment? | *Money and goods | The Mongols | 1240 | Destroyed Kyiv
exam: Ayo says tribute always means a thank-you. Is Ayo right? | No, it always means a payment of money | Yes, it always means a thank-you | Yes, but only in history lessons | *No, tribute can also mean money or goods a weaker people paid to a stronger ruler
